{"nodes": [{"id": "src_chrono_vehicle_cmakelists_chrono_vehicle", "label": "Chrono_vehicle Library Target", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_vehicle/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_chrono_vehicle_cmakelists_chrono_vehicle_irrlicht", "label": "Chrono_vehicle_irrlicht Target", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_vehicle/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_chrono_vehicle_cmakelists_chrono_vehicle_vsg", "label": "Chrono_vehicle_vsg Target", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "src/chrono_vehicle/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_chrono_vehicle_cmakelists_scm_gpu_backend", "label": "SCM GPU Ray-Casting Backend", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "src/chrono_vehicle/CMakeLists.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ships ON so hardware decides rather than a flag - an off-by-default accelerator is one most users never turn on; when the toolchain is absent it resolves to NONE and the CPU path runs, which is what a GPU-less machine would do anyway. The requirement is declared for the feature, not for Chrono::Vehicle, and is REQUIRES HIP because the kernels are HIP with no CUDA variant. Both HIP platforms are accepted since nothing here uses the ROCm-only hipCUB/rocPRIM/rocThrust that restrict Chrono::DEM and Chrono::FSI::SPH to amd. Unavailability is reported as IMPLIED and without OPTION, so an absent HIP toolchain is an ordinary fact about the machine rather than a warning, and the cache option is not force-disabled behind the user's back."}, {"id": "src_chrono_vehicle_cmakelists_opencrg_support", "label": "OpenCRG Terrain Support", "file_type": "concept", "source_f